[2026-09-02T19:11:33.839Z] [336e9441-a510-47fd-a252-db7fbfd79d2c] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=1 | score=61 | rootCause=The render follows the general sushi-commercial structure, but the actual execution is materially weaker than the plan: the reel has heavy repetition in the middle, no audible finished-commercial sound design, visible typography inconsistencies, and a hard black dead-end at the close instead of a polished end hold. The planned SFX/ramp/transition layer is not actually present in the render, so the edit feels flatter and less premium than the JSON suggests. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"CTA / Ending","timestamp_seconds":13.5,"problem":"The reel ends on black frames instead of a visible brand-safe CTA or hero hold. That breaks the commercial finish and makes the final action unclear.","fix":"Use the plated overhead hero frame as the full-duration end hold and keep the CTA on-screen through the last second; eliminate the black tail entirely."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Audio / Finishing","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The executable timeline promises music, SFX, and a finished commercial sound bed, but the render audit shows zero SFX events and the cut feels sonically flat.","fix":"Add real slice/impact/torch/CTA hits and ensure music ducks under the key beats; the edit needs tactile sonic punctuation to match the premium food visuals."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Pacing","timestamp_seconds":3,"problem":"The middle section lingers on similar prep visuals for too long, especially the repeated knife/prep/ingredient shots, which reduces momentum.","fix":"Collapse the middle to three distinct beats max: slice, ingredient placement, torch/payoff. Remove redundant hand-plating repetitions."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Typography","timestamp_seconds":4,"problem":"Text is readable but feels generic and repetitive; the on-screen phrases do not feel custom enough for a premium vertical commercial.","fix":"Use fewer words, stronger hierarchy, and one clean CTA treatment. Avoid stacking similar claims back-to-back."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Continuity","timestamp_seconds":10.5,"problem":"The ending reuses the opener without a meaningful visual progression, then abruptly drops to black, so the reel feels like it runs out of footage instead of landing a designed finish.","fix":"If reusing the opener as the CTA hold, change crop/zoom minimally and hold long enough to feel intentional, then end directly on the food frame—not black."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Brand","timestamp_seconds":10.5,"problem":"KAIRO branding is only implied through text; there is no visible in-frame restaurant brand or logo, so the ad relies entirely on captions.","fix":"Keep the text, but make the CTA unmistakable and specific; if possible, use the cleanest frame with maximum negative space and strongest brand name prominence."}]
